<article class="election-results" data-pagefind-body>
  <h1>November 3, 2026 results</h1>
  <p>Tuesday, November 3, 2026, is Election Day. Polls are open 7 a.m. to 7 p.m. Central time. <a href="{{ election2026.links.sosDates }}">{{ election2026.links.sosDatesLabel }}</a>. <a href="{{ election2026.links.currentElection }}">{{ election2026.links.currentElectionLabel }}</a>.</p>
  <p>Travis County says a voter may cast a ballot at any polling site in the county. <a href="{{ election2026.links.pollingLocations }}">{{ election2026.links.pollingLocationsLabel }}</a>. <a href="{{ election2026.links.electionDaySites }}">{{ election2026.links.electionDaySitesLabel }}</a>.</p>
  <p>The county voter lookup shows the ballot for a voter's address. <a href="{{ election2026.links.voterLookup }}">{{ election2026.links.voterLookupLabel }}</a>.</p>
  <p>The county results list did not include this election at {{ election2026.asOfDisplay }}. Each measure below reads Results not yet posted. <a href="{{ election2026.links.resultsPage }}">{{ election2026.links.resultsPageLabel }}</a>. <a href="{{ election2026.links.resultsEnr }}">{{ election2026.links.resultsEnrLabel }}</a>.</p>
  <p>No endorsements. Hours and the longer voting guide are on <a href="/vote-2026/">Vote 2026</a>.</p>

  <h2>Measures</h2>
  {% for measure in election2026.measures %}
  <section class="measure" id="{{ measure.id }}">
    <h3>{{ measure.ballotTitle }}</h3>
    <p>{{ measure.summary }}. <a href="{{ measure.source }}">{{ measure.sourceLabel }}</a>.</p>
    <p class="status">{{ measure.result.status }}.</p>
    {% if measure.result.yes != null and measure.result.no != null %}
    <p>Yes {{ measure.result.yes }}. No {{ measure.result.no }}.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if measure.result.outcome %}
    <p>{{ measure.ballotTitle }} is recorded as {{ measure.result.outcome }}.</p>
    {% endif %}
    <p>As of {{ measure.result.asOfDisplay }}, {{ measure.ballotTitle }}. <a href="{{ measure.result.source }}">{{ measure.result.sourceLabel }}</a>.</p>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}
</article>
